      "evidence": "Independent current review of the covariance Statement, all six proof steps, batch-44 contract/manifest, def-lorentz-map-and-lorentz-group Definition, and boost-factorization Statement/Proof confirms that no group topology is specified for the strong-continuity claim. The published algebraic definition makes no topological promise. A sound repair needs the matrix-subspace topology on SO+(1,3), continuity of the induced quotient action in that topology, and a checked Fock extension. The compact-support/near-apex argument is a plausible local closure, but cannot define a topology retroactively and the producer is outside batch-52 edit authority. Owner must route and independently review the batch-44 supplier repair, then resolve its consumer uses. Sources consulted: exact local carriers and Tong Chapter 6 \u00a7\u00a76.2.1\u20136.2.2; no textbook substitutes for the missing local definition.",
