      "evidence": "The exact boost-factorization Statement defines active boosts with positive sinh terms. Current covariance proof 2.1 correctly has omega prime=gamma(omega+beta n dot k), k prime=k+(gamma-1)(n dot k)n+gamma beta omega n and Jacobian omega prime/omega. Thus the reported older minus-sign attribution would be nonfatal and is absent from current bytes; inverse boosts would give the older formulas. However the reader could not bind the original observed bytes to pre/current snapshots. No explicit owner authorization disposing of that historical-byte gap is available in this dispatch. Independently checked the current producer proof, contract and manifest, but that cannot prove what historical bytes said or authorize historical closure. Owner must recover the observed carrier or explicitly authorize the historical disposition; preserve the original report and uncertainty. No current repair or false-positive verdict is claimed.",
